  -> One day, a little bird could not fly. It was sad. The bird had a bad wing. A big bird saw the little bird and wanted to help. The big bird had a plan to make the little bird happy. / The big bird told the little bird to touch it with its good wing. The little bird did as the big bird said. The little bird touched the little bird's bad wing. The little bird felt better. They became good friends. / The big bird also helped the little bird. It shared its food with the little bird. They both felt happy. The little bird could fly again. The little bird and the big bird were friends forever. They played together in the big green park.

